{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>When she has a discharge.</b> One might think from any of her organs — therefore Scripture says ״וְהִיא גִּלְּתָה אֶת מְקוֹר דָּמֶיהָ״ — blood defiles only that which comes from the source." "<b>Her discharge shall be blood in her flesh.</b> Her discharge is not called a discharge for defilement unless it is red — as it is written (Leviticus 19)." "<b>Her menstruation.</b> As in ״וּמִתֵּבֵל יְנִדֻּהוּ״ (Job 18) — that she is banished from the touch of any person." "<b>She shall be in her menstruation.</b> Even if she saw only a first sighting (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:37.261252331Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}